    "content": "## Engineering Barrier Protection for Dehydrated Allium Ingredients\n\nDehydrated onion powder (*Allium cepa*) is one of the most hygroscopic food ingredients in commercial trade. Because onions naturally contain high concentrations of low-molecular-weight sugars (fructose, glucose, and sucrose) and fructooligosaccharides, dried onion particles act as aggressive moisture magnets.\n\nIf exposed to ambient air with relative humidity above 60% for even a few hours, onion powder begins to adsorb water vapor. This triggers glass-transition surface plasticization: the sugars dissolve, particle surfaces become sticky, and the entire consignment fuses into an unworkable, rock-solid block.\n\nAt **AVANI AGRO FOODS**, we implement an engineered barrier packaging protocol to ensure our export consignments reach overseas warehouses in free-flowing condition. This guide details packaging specifications and warehouse storage rules.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The Anatomy of Export-Grade Onion Packaging\n\n```\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| THE AVANI DUAL-BARRIER ONION EXPORT PACKAGING SYSTEM                          |\n|                                                                               |\n| 1. INNER BARRIER: 50–70 Micron Virgin Low-Density Polyethylene (LDPE) Liner   |\n|    • Tinted Food-Grade Blue for instant visual contamination detection        |\n|    • Hermetically heat-sealed or twisted and tightly cable-tied               |\n|                                                                               |\n| 2. OUTER BARRIER: Heavy-Duty 5-Ply / 7-Ply Virgin Kraft Corrugated Carton     |\n|    • Bursting strength > 14 kg/cm²; crush-resistant under pallet stacking     |\n|    • Clear indelible export markings, batch codes, and origin labeling        |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Packaging Formats Compared: Cartons vs. Multi-Wall Bags\n\n| Specification Feature | 20kg / 25kg Corrugated Export Cartons | 25kg Multi-Wall Kraft Paper Sacks |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Material Construction** | 5-Ply or 7-Ply Rigid Corrugated Board | 3 to 4-Ply Bleached/Natural Kraft Paper |\n| **Moisture Vapor Barrier**| Superior (Complete protection with blue liner)| High (Heat-sealed inner poly liner) |\n| **Puncture & Forklift Resistance**| Excellent (Thick rigid corrugated walls) | Moderate (Susceptible to tearing on nails)|\n| **Pallet Stacking Stability** | Outstanding (Square box edges interlock evenly)| Good (Requires tight shrink-wrapping) |\n| **Pallet Space Efficiency** | 100% cubic utilization on Euro/US pallets | High container stuffing weight yield |\n| **Standard Net Weight** | **20.0 kg Net** (Preferred) / 25.0 kg Net | **25.0 kg Net** |\n\n*Procurement Tip:* We strongly recommend **20 kg corrugated cartons** for international ocean shipments. Cartons stack with perfect vertical column strength, preventing the bottom tiers from compressing under the weight of 10-tier pallet stacks during heavy sea motion.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Container Stuffing & Maritime Moisture Protection\n\nDuring maritime voyages across tropical ocean lanes, temperature fluctuations trigger condensation inside steel container ceilings (\"container rain\"). If condensation drips onto packaging, water stains can ruin cartons.\n- **Container Desiccant Poles:** AVANI AGRO FOODS places heavy-duty calcium chloride desiccant hanging poles (absorbing up to 300% dry weight) along container walls.\n- **Top Pallet Plastic Sheeting:** Every pallet receives a waterproof polyethylene top cover prior to stretch-wrapping to deflect any falling moisture.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Destination Warehouse Storage Protocols\n\nFollow these 4 operational rules to guarantee a full 24-month shelf life:\n1. **Maintain Controlled Warehouse Temperature:** Keep warehouse temperature strictly between **16°C and 22°C** (60°F–72°F). Storage above 30°C accelerates non-enzymatic Maillard browning, turning pinkish powder dull brown.\n2. **Relative Humidity (RH) Limits:** Maintain ambient warehouse humidity strictly below **50% to 55%**.\n3. **Off-Ground Clearance:** Keep palletized stock on warehouse racking or wooden/plastic pallets at least 30 cm away from exterior walls. Never place cartons directly on concrete flooring.\n4. **Resealing Discipline:** When opening a 20kg carton for partial production, immediately expel headspace air and tightly cable-tie or heat-seal the blue poly liner.\n\n---\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\n\n### Why is the inner polyethylene liner tinted blue?\nIn industrial food manufacturing, blue is the universal color for food-contact packaging. Because blue is virtually non-existent in natural food matrices, if a shred of the liner is accidentally cut by a warehouse box cutter, it is instantly visible to QA personnel and optical inspection cameras.\n\n### Can onion powder that has caked be salvaged?\nLightly clumped powder can sometimes be broken up by gentle mechanical sifting. However, if severe caking has occurred due to moisture penetration, the internal moisture content has exceeded 8%, creating microbial risks and irreversible flavor degradation. Prevention through barrier packaging is the only reliable solution.\n\n---\n\n## Secure Your Packaging Specifications\n\nProtect your food ingredient supply chain from moisture risks.\n- Review technical specifications in our [Red Onion Powder Catalog](/catalog/red-onion-powder).\n- Learn about our quality workflows in [Export Process Walkthrough](/export-process).\n- [Submit Your Packaging Requirements](/contact?product=onion&type=quote) to Trade Coordinator Sachin Shinde.\n"
