    "content": "## Mastering Import Compliance for Dehydrated Allium Consignments\n\nIn the global trade of agricultural food ingredients, administrative and documentation precision is just as critical as physical product quality. Customs and biosecurity agencies across the United States, European Union, United Kingdom, and United Arab Emirates enforce computerized risk-targeting algorithms. A clerical typo on a Bill of Lading, a missing phytosanitary declaration, or an ambiguous product description can result in container holds, expensive port demurrage fees, and formal border rejections.\n\nAt **AVANI AGRO FOODS**, our trade coordination desk maintains flawless documentation standards. Every export consignment is supported by an airtight, legally authenticated document dossier.\n\nThis guide provides international buyers and customs brokers with the complete checklist of required documents and exact verification rules.\n\n---\n\n## The Master Export Documentation Dossier\n\n```\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| THE COMPLETE RED ONION IMPORT DOCUMENTATION PACKET                            |\n| 1. Commercial Invoice (Itemized, HS Code 07122000, Signed & Company Stamped)  |\n| 2. Packing List (Net, Gross, Tare Weights, Container & Seal Identification)   |\n| 3. Clean On-Board Ocean Bill of Lading (Negotiable Original or Telex Release) |\n| 4. Federal Phytosanitary Certificate (Issued by Ministry of Agriculture, India)|\n| 5. Certificate of Origin (Issued by Chamber of Commerce / EIC)                 |\n| 6. Independent NABL-Accredited Batch Certificate of Analysis (COA)             |\n| 7. Non-GMO, Allergen-Free & Non-Irradiation Manufacturer Declarations          |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n## Document-by-Document Verification Rules\n\n### 1. The Commercial Invoice\n- **Exporter & Consignee Identity:** Explicitly lists AVANI AGRO FOODS (Latur, Maharashtra, India) and the exact registered corporate entity of the buyer.\n- **Harmonized System (HS) Code:** Must clearly declare **0712.20.00** for dehydrated onion powder.\n- **Incoterm & Port Notation:** Explicitly declares Incoterms 2020 terms (e.g., *\"FOB Nhava Sheva (JNPT Mumbai)\"* or *\"CIF Los Angeles Port, USA\"*).\n- **Batch Serialization:** References the specific manufacturing batch numbers matching physical cartons.\n\n### 2. The Packing List\n- **Detailed Weight Audit:** Itemized breakdown of number of cartons, net weight (e.g., 20.0 kg/carton), gross weight (e.g., 21.2 kg/carton), and total tare weight.\n- **Container & Seal Numbers:** Container identification (e.g., MEDU1234567) and high-security bolt seal numbers must match physical ocean container seals exactly.\n\n### 3. The Clean On-Board Ocean Bill of Lading (B/L)\n- **Shipped on Board Date:** Validates that the cargo has physically loaded aboard the vessel prior to Letter of Credit expiry.\n- **Port of Loading:** Nhava Sheva / Jawaharlal Nehru Port (INNSA).\n- **Consignee / Notify Party:** Formatted in strict compliance with buyer banking or customs broker instructions.\n\n### 4. The Federal Phytosanitary Certificate\n- **Issuing Authority:** Directorate of Plant Protection, Quarantine & Storage, Ministry of Agriculture, Government of India.\n- **Biosecurity Certification:** Certifies that the agricultural commodity has been thoroughly inspected and found free from quarantine pests (such as storage beetles, mites, and parasitic nematodes).\n- **Critical Verification:** Must be issued prior to or on the exact date of vessel departure.\n\n### 5. The Certificate of Origin (COO)\n- **Issuing Authority:** Authorized Indian Chamber of Commerce or Export Inspection Council (EIC).\n- **Customs Role:** Essential for verifying Indian origin and securing preferential duty rates where applicable.\n\n### 6. The Independent Batch Certificate of Analysis (COA)\n- Must be issued by an independent, NABL-accredited (ISO/IEC 17025) testing laboratory (e.g., SGS, Eurofins, Vimta Labs).\n- Must reference the exact batch numbers printed on physical shipping cartons.\n\n---\n\n## Market-Specific Customs Requirements\n\n| Destination Market | Regulatory Agency | Mandatory Specialized Documentation |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **United States** | US FDA / US Customs (CBP) | • Importer Security Filing (ISF 10+2) 24h prior to vessel loading<br>• FDA Prior Notice Confirmation Number<br>• Foreign Supplier Verification Program (FSVP) records |\n| **European Union** | EU Member State Customs / EFSA | • TRACES NT digital declaration<br>• Sulfur Dioxide (SO2) level verification certificate<br>• Maximum Residue Limit (MRL) pesticide clearance |\n| **United Kingdom** | UK Border Force / FSA | • IPAFFS digital pre-notification<br>• UK Customs Declaration Service (CDS) clearance |\n| **United Arab Emirates** | Dubai Municipality / ESMA | • Dubai Municipality FoodWatch Registration<br>• Certified Halal Conformity Certificate<br>• Bilingual Arabic/English carton markings |\n\n---\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\n\n### Can export documentation be surrendered electronically via Telex Release?\nYes. Where payment terms permit (e.g., wire transfer upon copy of draft B/L), an electronic **Telex Release (Express Bill of Lading)** eliminates physical courier delays, enabling your destination customs broker to clear cargo days before the vessel docks.\n\n### What is the import duty on dehydrated red onion powder?\nIn the United States and European Union, dehydrated allium products from India generally enter duty-free (0%) under normal trade relations. In the UAE and GCC, standard customs tariffs are 5%.\n\n---\n\n## Experience Seamless Trade Execution\n\nPartner with an Indian trade coordinator dedicated to flawless compliance.\n- Learn more in our [Export Compliance Overview](/export-compliance).\n- Review our full product line in the [B2B Export Catalog](/catalog).\n- [Contact Sachin Shinde](/contact?product=onion&type=quote) to discuss custom documentation requirements for your destination market.\n"
