    "content": "## Why Precision in Your RFQ Secures Sharper Commercial Pricing\n\nIn international agricultural trade, sending a vague, two-line inquiry such as *\"Please send best price for 1 container of onion powder\"* places the supplier in a difficult commercial position. Without knowing your required mesh particle size, moisture limits, packaging format, destination port, or delivery timeline, exporters must include substantial risk buffers in their pricing.\n\nConversely, issuing a well-structured, professional **Request for Quotation (RFQ)** immediately signals that your company is a serious commercial buyer with defined technical specifications. Exporters prioritize your inquiry, provide their most competitive unit pricing, and deliver accurate shipping schedules within 24 hours.\n\nAt **AVANI AGRO FOODS**, we manage international procurement inquiries every week. This guide provides international buyers with a proven RFQ framework to secure transparent, competitive, and technically accurate commercial quotations for dehydrated Red Onion powder.\n\n---\n\n## The Essential Parameters of a Professional B2B RFQ\n\nTo receive an itemized, binding Proforma Quotation, include these 7 key commercial parameters:\n\n```\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| 1. Product Identity: 100% Dehydrated Red Onion Powder (Allium cepa L.)        |\n| 2. Required Mesh Particle Size: 80–100 Mesh (Fine) or 60–80 Mesh (Granular)   |\n| 3. Target Commercial Volume: Trial consignment (1–2 MT) vs 20ft FCL (~14 MT)  |\n| 4. Packaging Specification: 20kg Corrugated Cartons vs 25kg Kraft Paper Sacks  |\n| 5. Required Incoterms 2020: FOB Nhava Sheva (JNPT) or CIF Destination Port    |\n| 6. Analytical & Testing Standards: Independent NABL COA, SO2 limits, MRLs     |\n| 7. Target Shipping Window & Destination Seaport: Target sailing date          |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n## RFQ Copy-and-Paste Template for Buyers\n\nUse this proven template when issuing inquiries to AVANI AGRO FOODS or prospective suppliers:\n\n```email\nSubject: RFQ: Dehydrated Red Onion Powder — [Your Company Name] — [Target Volume]\n\nDear Sachin Shinde / AVANI AGRO FOODS Trade Coordination Desk,\n\nOur procurement team is currently reviewing supplier partnerships for export-grade \ndehydrated Red Onion powder. Please provide a formal commercial quotation based on \nthe following technical and commercial parameters:\n\n1. PRODUCT SPECIFICATIONS:\n   • Botanical Identity: 100% Dehydrated Red Onion Powder (Allium cepa)\n   • Particle Size: 80–100 Mesh (≥ 95% pass through 150 microns)\n   • Moisture Guarantee: ≤ 6.0% Maximum\n   • Acid-Insoluble Ash: ≤ 0.5% Maximum (Zero sand / silica)\n   • Sulfur Dioxide (SO2): Non-Detectable (< 10 ppm) or < 50 ppm\n   • Microbial Standards: Salmonella Negative/25g, E. coli Negative/10g, TPC ≤ 100,000 CFU/g\n   • Heavy Metal Limits: Lead < 2.0 ppm, Cadmium < 1.0 ppm, ETO-Free (< 0.05 mg/kg)\n\n2. COMMERCIAL VOLUME & ORDER STRUCTURE:\n   • Initial Consignment: [e.g., 2,000 kg (LCL/Palletized) OR 1 x 20ft FCL (~13,000 kg)]\n   • Projected Annual Volume: [e.g., 25 to 75 Metric Tons / Year]\n\n3. PACKAGING & PALLETIZATION:\n   • Inner Packaging: Heavy-duty 50-micron blue virgin LDPE liner, heat-sealed\n   • Outer Packaging: [20 kg 5-Ply Corrugated Export Cartons / 25 kg Multi-Wall Kraft Sacks]\n   • Palletization: ISPM-15 certified heat-treated wooden pallets, shrink-wrapped with corner boards\n\n4. INCOTERMS & DESTINATION PORT:\n   • Please quote BOTH: FOB Nhava Sheva (JNPT Mumbai, India) AND CIF [Your Destination Port]\n   • Destination Seaport: [e.g., New York (USNYC), Felixstowe (GBFXT), Jebel Ali (AEJEA), Rotterdam (NLRTM)]\n\n5. QUALITY VERIFICATION & SAMPLES:\n   • Please attach a recent Certificate of Analysis (COA) from an independent NABL lab.\n   • Advise availability and procedure for dispatching a 250g evaluation sample via courier.\n\nWe look forward to receiving your formal Proforma Quote and technical data sheet.\n\nBest regards,\n\n[Your Name]\n[Your Title / Procurement Director]\n[Company Name]\n[Country / Corporate Website / Direct Phone Number]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Verifying Supplier Quotations: 4 Key Checks\n\nWhen you receive a Proforma Quotation, verify that the supplier itemizes:\n1. **Quotation Validity Window:** Raw onion prices fluctuate seasonally in Maharashtra. A standard commercial quote is typically valid for 14 to 30 days.\n2. **Gross vs. Net Weight Calculation:** Confirms you are not paying product rates for packaging tare weight.\n3. **Production Lead Time:** Explicitly states the business days required from deposit receipt to port CFS gate-in.\n4. **Third-Party Lab Inclusion:** Verifies that the cost of independent NABL-accredited testing is included in the unit price.\n\n---\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\n\n### How quickly does AVANI AGRO FOODS deliver Proforma Quotations?\nOur trade coordination desk delivers formal, itemized Proforma Quotations within **24 business hours** of receiving your structured technical inquiry.\n\n### Can I request mixed containerloads of both Moringa and Onion powder?\nYes. We coordinate consolidated 20ft containerloads containing palletized lots of both Moringa leaf powder and Red Onion powder, enabling buyers to optimize freight while testing multiple product lines.\n\n---\n\n## Request Your Official Bulk Quotation Now\n\nPut your sourcing requirements directly into the hands of our trade coordination team.\n- Review technical specifications in our [Red Onion Powder Catalog](/catalog/red-onion-powder).\n- Compare with our [Moringa Powder Export Catalog](/catalog/moringa-powder).\n- [Submit Your Official Sourcing Request](/contact?product=onion&type=quote) to Trade Coordinator Sachin Shinde at AVANI AGRO FOODS.\n"
